It has been a couple of years since I last posted this list, and, as
I am also nearing completion of one of the tricks, it seemed a good time
to send it around again. As always, discussion is welcome.

I have also made a simple HTML version of the list available at:
http://www.thinksystem.net/nethack

The latest version of the semi-exhaustive list of

  Stupid Ascension Tricks

This is a list of things you could do on your way to an ascension. Be
warned that the vast majority of them are stupid. Any smart player 
would just do anything that they could to ascend.

This has every checked-for conduct, I think every voluntary conduct 
I've seen mentioned, and a bunch of other things. It started after 
realizing that the conducts Nethack checks for are good, but nowhere 
near complete. (It checks for not eating food, but not for not 
quaffing potions.)

Each trick has a difficulty rating that I've given it (so yes, it is
quite subjective). The difficulty is divided into three areas, 
Patience, Luck, and Planning. Patience means that about all you need 
is the willingness to sit there and type the keys enough times. Luck 
means that the RNG needs to smile on you at least a bit. Planning 
means that you have to consider the order that you are doing things
in the game and have preparation complete before starting a new 
segment. All three given on a scale from Trivial through Slight, 
Moderate, Significant, and Heroic. They are also based on the 
assumption that the player could probably get a game
through to an ascension if they were careful.

The only significant change from version 0.4 is that all of the 
artifact-related tricks are now collected in section 34 of the list
and the Miscellaneous ones have been moved to section 35.

-Harold Hill


